ng T1134.004; GUID before pid; original spelling).\nATT&CK when no attack= in plan: role table in lib.scripts.role_attack; host-language sub-ids T1059.001 PS .002 AppleScript\n .003 cmd .004 unix shell .005 VB .006 python .007 JS .010 AutoHotKey/AutoIt .011 Lua; v=3 used parent T1059 (C#/Groovy/GHA/NSIS).\nEQUIVALENCE (D16 plan_canonical) / CI-PERSISTENCE (D21 rows 78/79) / INSTALLER setup-vs-payload (D22) prompts: flavour.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\nBuilt by the nightly prebuild (dropped from the queue, still usable from lib/): D16-D20 nights (see git history) and D21 night\ngha-trigger-trust-model, ci-schedule-persistence-model, ci-yaml-sibling-route, github-action-definition-route,\nci-expression-injection-secrets, k8s-helm-manifest-route, git-repo-hooks-route, launchd-plist-route. Given up (2 attempts):\npython-exec-onion-static, evidence-type-router, file-registry-telemetry-reconcile, build-manifest-hooks. Pending after 1\nunfinished attempt (cost 0): cloud-iac-userdata-route, yaml-scalar-carrier-twists. Prebuild gate: lib imports limited to hctf/prebuild.py ALLOWED_IMPORTS (stdlib parsers + Crypto/cryptography/dpkt/\nEvtx/pefile/olefile/dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D23: the D22 theme the bytes did not carry yet\n(installer setup-vs-payload actions + handoffs), an NSIS carrier twist (`!define`/StrCpy appends/`$\\` escapes), the next\ninstaller language (Inno Setup), WiX/MSI custom actions; then compiled installers, OS package scripts, package-manager\nmanifests, IaC, YAML twists, Electron/Squirrel.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"installer-action-model\", \"concept\": \"installer scripts: separate real setup actions from payload behaviour and list every cross-language handoff (NSIS / Inno / WiX)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 prompt 'Separate the real setup actions from the modeled payload behavior, and recover every cross-language handoff' + base id `installer-script-chain` -- D22 bytes carried only Name/OutFile/Section/StrCpy, so a variant/next day adding real installer statements would ask new suffixes (`-setup-actions`, `-payload-actions`, `-handoff`, `-handoff-count`, `-next-stage`). i\n  {\"id\": \"nsis-string-define-fold\", \"concept\": \"NSIS carrier twists: !define/${X} substitution, StrCpy appends, $\\\\ escapes, alternate quotes and comment forms\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D22 NSIS carriers were plain (`StrCpy $0 \\\"<data>\\\"`); the D18/D19-style twist on the newest language would hide the descriptor in NSIS string semantics. nsis_strings(src)->{var/define: value}: `!define NAME \\\"..\\\"` / `!define /date` / `!define /math` (ignore), `${NAME}` substitution (recursive, defines may be redefined with `!undef`), `StrCpy $0 \\\"part1\\\"` then `StrCpy $0 \\\"$0part2\\\"` /\n  {\"id\": \"inno-setup-iss-route\", \"concept\": \"Inno Setup `.iss` scripts (sections + Pascal Script [Code]) as the next installer language\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Installer sibling of D22 NSIS (cf. D12 AutoIt -> D17 AutoHotkey, D20 Jenkins -> D21 GHA). Verify lib.codec.v3_plan/find_codecs on a fixture battery wrapping D22-style plans in .iss: marker in `;` (section comments) and `//`, `{ }`, `(* *)` (Pascal [Code]); descriptor forms `const descriptor_<8hex> = '..';`, `var Descriptor: String; .. Descriptor := '..' + '..';` (Pascal `''` escape inside single quotes, `#13#10\n  {\"id\": \"wix-msi-custom-action-route\", \"concept\": \"WiX `.wxs` source and built `.msi` databases: custom-action scripts as cross-language handoffs\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"MSI is the native Windows installer; its custom actions are inline VBScript/JScript (types 37/38/53/54 = script in property/Binary, 5/6 = JScript/VBS from Binary, 34/50 = EXE command lines). wix_actions(src)->[{id, type, script_lang, body, exe_command, sequence, condition}] over `<CustomAction Id Script=\\\"vbscript|jscript\\\">` CDATA bodies, `BinaryKey`+`<Binary SourceFile>` (resolve to a sibling membe\n  {\"id\": \"nsis-compiled-installer-extract\", \"concept\": \"compiled NSIS (and Inno) setup EXEs: recover the embedded script strings and files without running them\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"A timed variant or the next day may ship the BUILT `huntress-<8hex>.exe` named by D22's OutFile. NSIS: PE overlay holds firstheader (flags u32, `EF BE AD DE`, `NullsoftInst`, header_size, archive_size), then the header block (u32 length with high bit = compressed; zlib raw deflate / bzip2 / LZMA `5D 00 00` props, or one solid stream) holding the section/entry tables and a string table (U\n  {\"id\": \"linux-package-maintainer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"deb / rpm / PKGBUILD / APKBUILD maintainer scripts as installer-chain carriers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Linux side of 'installer script chain'. pkg_scripts(name, data)->[{format, hook (preinst|postinst|prerm|postrm|config|triggers|%pre|%post|%preun|%postun|%pretrans|%posttrans|%trigger*|pre_install|post_install|post_upgrade), interpreter, body}]: `.deb` = ar (`!<arch>\\\\n`, 60-byte headers) -> `control.tar.gz|xz|zst` (tarfile handles gz/xz; zst -> report) -> scripts; `.rpm` = 96-byte lead `ED AB EE DB`, signature \n  {\"id\": \"macos-pkg-installer-scripts\", \"concept\": \"macOS flat `.pkg` (xar) Distribution JavaScript and preinstall/postinstall scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Installer sibling on macOS (cf. D13 AppleScript). macpkg_scripts(data)->[{path, kind (distribution_js|preinstall|postinstall|payload), lang, body}]: xar header (`xar!`, u16 header size, u16 version, u64 toc_len_compressed, u64 toc_len_uncompressed, u32 checksum alg), zlib TOC XML -> <file> entries with <data><offset><length><encoding style=application/x-gzip|x-bzip2>, heap after TOC; `Distribution` XML `<install\n  {\"id\": \"package-manager-install-manifests\", \"concept\": \"Chocolatey / NuGet / Scoop / winget / Homebrew / MSIX-ClickOnce install manifests and their install scripts\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Package-manager installers run scripts too. pkgmgr_scripts(members)->[{manager, hook, lang, body_or_url}]: `.nupkg` (zip) `tools/chocolateyInstall.ps1|chocolateyBeforeModify.ps1|chocolateyUninstall.ps1`, NuGet `tools/install.ps1|init.ps1`, `.nuspec` XML; Scoop JSON `pre_install`/`post_install`/`installer.script`/`uninstaller.script` (string OR array of lines -> join with \\\\n -> Pow\n  {\"id\": \"cloud-iac-userdata-route\", \"concept\": \"IaC templates with embedded scripts: Terraform local-exec/user_data, CloudFormation UserData Fn::Base64, ARM/Bicep deploymentScripts, Ansible shell tasks\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"After CI, infra-as-code is the next 'build that runs code' surface. iac_scripts(name, src)->[{resource, field, lang, body}]: Terraform HCL `provisioner \\\"local-exec\\\" { command = <<-EOT .. EOT interpreter = [\\\"pwsh\\\",\\\"-c\\\"] }`, `user_data = base64encode(..)`/`filebase64(..)`/`templatefile`, `data \\\"external\\\" { program = [..] }`; CloudFormation\n  {\"id\": \"solver-lib-v3-fallback\", \"concept\": \"carried solve.py must ask lib.codec.v3_plan when its own v=3 read yields nothing\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19: lib.codec.v3_plan already decoded the ASPX escaped-nested carrier, but the carried solve.py `_v3` only used its own V3_MARK/descriptor regexes, so 11 ids went planless and the race harness probed guesses. The D20 solver-authoring pass: in analyse_v3, if no candidate peels to `v=`, call lib.codec.v3_plan(text) (and lib.codec.find_codecs) before giving up; log which reader won. Same for D18 SPLIT (now in both). STILL OP\n  {\"id\": \"php-cli\", \"concept\": \"PHP CLI for lint/tokenize\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y php-cli  (php -l, token_get_all; never run fixtures). PHP is a carried language since D8.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"lua-unluac\", \"concept\": \"Lua interpreter + bytecode decompiler\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y lua5.4 luajit ; unluac.jar from https://sourceforge.net/projects/unluac/ into tools/unluac (java 25 installed) with bin/unluac wrapper. Needed if a luac-compiled carrier variant of the D9 Lua fixtures appears.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\", \"concept\": \"XML/CAB/YAML helpers\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y xsltproc cabextract ; yq: pip install yq into .venv (jq wrapper; jq installed). xsltproc only for --noout lint, never to apply a stylesheet.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"electron-asar-squirrel-route\", \"concept\": \"Electron `app.asar` archives and Squirrel/NuGet updater packages as JS carriers\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Installer-delivered Electron apps hide Node JS in `resources/app.asar`: Chromium pickle header (u32 4, u32 header_size, u32 pickle size, u32 json_len, JSON `{files:{name:{offset,size,unpacked?}}}`, file data after header padded to 4) -> list + extract `package.json` `main`, `*.js`; Squirrel `RELEASES` + `.nupkg` (zip) with `lib/net45/*.exe` and `Update.exe --processStart` command lines. asar_files(data)->{path: by\n  {\"id\": \"yaml-scalar-carrier-twists\", \"concept\": \"YAML-specific carrier mutations for the D21 language: block/folded scalars, anchors/aliases, tags, escapes, multi-doc\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D21 carriers were a one-line quoted scalar; the next twist on a YAML language (as D18/D19 twisted theirs) would hide the descriptor in YAML semantics. yaml_scalar(src, key)->decoded text honoring: literal `|`/`|-`/`|+` (keep newlines) vs folded `>`/`>-` (lines JOIN WITH A SPACE -- strip spaces before peeling hex/base64), indentation indicators `|2`, double-quoted escapes (`\\\\x41\n  {\"id\": \"leaf-ext-list\", \"concept\": \"nested-zip sniff skips unknown leaf extensions\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"_LEAF_EXT in solve.py still lacks .lua .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi (and future .tcl .r .kts .java .jsp .ipynb .go .rs .awk .tf .xsl .reg .inf .iss .wxs). Speed only (~1 s); prefer sniffing PK magic over an extension list.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"new-synthetic-label-family\", \"concept\": \"code-shape labels for a new language (D2-D7 style)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Polyglot days have been plan-verbatim since D8, but an 'advanced <lang>' set (like bash-advanced) would bring feature/primitive or control/style labels, and OLD label families can flip regime (batch expansion D15/D16). Apply playbook NAMING LAWS; probe one field per submit; check started_at/run_for_time first.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"family-name-underscore\", \"concept\": \"host-type families like polyglot-github_actions / host-<profile>-<lang>\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Keep the longest-known-suffix field parse; derive the family prefix from the contract ids, never from the file stem (D14 msbuild_xml). D17 added `polyglot-auto_hotkey` (campaign AUTO_HOTKEY-, url host auto_hotkey-..). D18: `polyglot-google_apps_script` (campaign GOOGLE_APPS_SCRIPT-, url host google_apps_script-..) while its host file is hyphenated `host-google-docs-sidebar-google-apps-script` (profile google_docs_sidebar). D19: `po\n  {\"id\": \"tcl-r-interpreters\", \"concept\": \"tclsh / Rscript for syntax checks\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"sudo apt-get install -y tcl (small); r-base-core is ~100 MB, install only on an R day. Static reading is enough for v=3 plans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"applescript-scpt\", \"concept\": \"compiled AppleScript (.scpt FasdUAS) disassembly\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Jinmo/applescript-disassembler into tools/ (pure python). D13 shipped source .applescript only; a compiled variant would hide the marker in UTF-16/MacRoman strings.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"js-deob-extras\", \"concept\": \"synchrony / JSFuck decoding\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"npm i deobfuscator (synchrony CLI) into tools/npm; webcrack (installed) already handles obfuscator.io; JSFuck/JJencode via js_sandbox capture of the final call.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ps-deob-modules\", \"concept\": \"PowerDecode / PSDecode for pwsh\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"git clone https://github.com/Malandrone/PowerDecode and https://github.com/R3MRUM/PSDecode into tools/ (pwsh 7.6.6 installed). refinery ps1 covers most; these add layer-by-layer IEX override tracing.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"xlm-standalone\", \"concept\": \"XLMMacroDeobfuscator CLI\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python XLMMacroDeobfuscator  (refinery xlmdeobf is an inlined port and already works; standalone gives --sort-formulas/--extract-only).\"},","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"persistedOutputPath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/2434f37c-0f23-47a1-8221-7c3852d69d0d/tool-results/bwb8lpjlu.txt","persistedOutputSize":50843},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CAmyZKTLEJjz23BqpWHPi4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
