{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgKFgNibEtS8C5853EwjJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015sG8Z8CVLMH3cWrRArEcaD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed\n  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;\n  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced\n  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt\n  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->\n  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +\n  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> **GDScript `.gd` (d23,\n  1461 = +44, 157 members, no host, no Bash)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the\n  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp\n  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->\n  NSIS; **D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,\n  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are\n  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20\n  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus\n  to find the level that doesn't belong\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"\n  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets\n  D22 (8502), **7 sets D23 (10465 ids)** in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is\n  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the\n  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT\n5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**. Auto cases D20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M\n1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4) are value re-rolls; D23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.\n- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members\n  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,\n  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for\n  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch\n  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python\n  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,\n  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first\n  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/\n  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python\n  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,\n  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.\n  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation\n  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;\n  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,\n  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the\n  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the\n  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed\n  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.\n- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x\n  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,\n  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh), stage_count 2-8, python syntax/obfuscation new\n  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).\n  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per\n  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index\n  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,\n  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,\n  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,\n  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`\n  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const\n  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n  these as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. |\n| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\nReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\nescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\nSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\nmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\nthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\nSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\ns). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n**D23 Press Start to Decode (base `game-resource-loader`; 1461 ids = +44, 157 members)**: +4\n`polyglot-gdscript-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.gd` only (no host, no Bash). Artifact: 6-line Godot\nscripts -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<FRAG|HEX|B64|HB64>-<data>`, `extends RefCounted`, typed `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>:\nString = \"<same data>\"`, `func build_plan_<8hex>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`. Plans: `language=gdscript`,\ncampaign `GDSCRIPT-<8hex>`, url `https://gdscript-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-gdscript/.<16hex>.\nstage`, attack none/T1105/T1059, host_profile standalone; role independent of steps again (downloader with `decode_configuration\n>return_configuration`, benign_utility with `profile_host>..>dispatch_language`). **Single: carried solver CORRECT T+52 s, 0\nwrong, one submit.** The twist was in the TIMED modes: a reshaped contract (hashed members + per-file ids + composite fields +\n`LYR-` tags + re-rolled plan vocab + a cross-file `handoff-id`). TT b10c4da4: carried solver 593/1495 -> generalize workers\n(one died on prompt size) added `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> 1495/1495; first run 4 batch `-style` ids wrong (`..|percent`),\n~31 localize probes, live worker `call_double` -> **CORRECT T+14 min 16 s**. Mastery e24c070d (7 sets, 10465 ids) started\nbefore the fix generalized: 12 batch `-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1's value reused for sets 2-7) wrong, ~57 localize probes ->\nper-set handoff lookup + call_double on any pool -> **CORRECT T+11 min 9 s**. The prompt's \"level that doesn't belong\" was\nnever asked.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp; GHA/NSIS/GDScript polyglots `standalone`),\n  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D23 GDScript. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D23) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n- **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23 TT fixed `call_double` for the FrAg pool only; Mastery then lost 12 ids\n  on the same construct over other pools): generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance, then re-run all cases.\n- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D15-D16, D23): tabulate (construct, GM label) against every contract key AND\n  the asking field at once.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D23 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (chunks <= 500 answers / 512 KiB); pair\n  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D23): ten prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":217,"cache_read_input_tokens":147505,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":217},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2434f37c-0f23-47a1-8221-7c3852d69d0d","uuid":"6a8bf1fb-9bd7-47d9-84d7-488ccc36a29d","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:34:42.424Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFgNM2JjyvQsz4SpDBE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_015sG8Z8CVLMH3cWrRArEcaD":{"file_path":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed\n  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;\n  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced\n  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt\n  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->\n  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +\n  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> **GDScript `.gd` (d23,\n  1461 = +44, 157 members, no host, no Bash)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the\n  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp\n  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->\n  NSIS; **D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,\n  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are\n  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20\n  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus\n  to find the level that doesn't belong\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"\n  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets\n  D22 (8502), **7 sets D23 (10465 ids)** in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is\n  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the\n  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT\n5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**. Auto cases D20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M\n1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4) are value re-rolls; D23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.\n- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members\n  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,\n  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for\n  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch\n  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python\n  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,\n  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first\n  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/\n  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python\n  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,\n  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.\n  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation\n  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;\n  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,\n  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the\n  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the\n  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed\n  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.\n- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x\n  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,\n  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh), stage_count 2-8, python syntax/obfuscation new\n  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).\n  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per\n  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index\n  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,\n  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,\n  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,\n  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`\n  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const\n  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n  these as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. |\n| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\nReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\nescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\nSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\nmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\nthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\nSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\ns). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n**D23 Press Start to Decode (base `game-resource-loader`; 1461 ids = +44, 157 members)**: +4\n`polyglot-gdscript-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.gd` only (no host, no Bash). Artifact: 6-line Godot\nscripts -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<FRAG|HEX|B64|HB64>-<data>`, `extends RefCounted`, typed `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>:\nString = \"<same data>\"`, `func build_plan_<8hex>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`. Plans: `language=gdscript`,\ncampaign `GDSCRIPT-<8hex>`, url `https://gdscript-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-gdscript/.<16hex>.\nstage`, attack none/T1105/T1059, host_profile standalone; role independent of steps again (downloader with `decode_configuration\n>return_configuration`, benign_utility with `profile_host>..>dispatch_language`). **Single: carried solver CORRECT T+52 s, 0\nwrong, one submit.** The twist was in the TIMED modes: a reshaped contract (hashed members + per-file ids + composite fields +\n`LYR-` tags + re-rolled plan vocab + a cross-file `handoff-id`). TT b10c4da4: carried solver 593/1495 -> generalize workers\n(one died on prompt size) added `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> 1495/1495; first run 4 batch `-style` ids wrong (`..|percent`),\n~31 localize probes, live worker `call_double` -> **CORRECT T+14 min 16 s**. Mastery e24c070d (7 sets, 10465 ids) started\nbefore the fix generalized: 12 batch `-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1's value reused for sets 2-7) wrong, ~57 localize probes ->\nper-set handoff lookup + call_double on any pool -> **CORRECT T+11 min 9 s**. The prompt's \"level that doesn't belong\" was\nnever asked.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp; GHA/NSIS/GDScript polyglots `standalone`),\n  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D23 GDScript. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D23) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n- **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23 TT fixed `call_double` for the FrAg pool only; Mastery then lost 12 ids\n  on the same construct over other pools): generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance, then re-run all cases.\n- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D15-D16, D23): tabulate (construct, GM label) against every contract key AND\n  the asking field at once.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D23 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (chunks <= 500 answers / 512 KiB); pair\n  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D23): ten prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015sG8Z8CVLMH3cWrRArEcaD","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2434f37c-0f23-47a1-8221-7c3852d69d0d","uuid":"810d507f-c5c3-43ac-8f79-37b2dcc8e240","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:34:42.547Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/script-analysis.md","content":"# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)\n\nHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed\n  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;\n  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.\n- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is\n  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15\n  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced\n  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt\n  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->\n  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +\n  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> **GDScript `.gd` (d23,\n  1461 = +44, 157 members, no host, no Bash)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the\n  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp\n  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->\n  NSIS; **D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's.\n- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.\n  It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.\n  Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`\n  itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic\n  labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,\n  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are\n  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.\n- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20\n  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus\n  to find the level that doesn't belong\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"\n  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.\n- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets\n  D22 (8502), **7 sets D23 (10465 ids)** in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is\n  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the\n  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).\n\n## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\nEach miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT\n5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**. Auto cases D20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M\n1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4) are value re-rolls; D23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.\n- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members\n  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,\n  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for\n  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch\n  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python\n  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,\n  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first\n  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/\n  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python\n  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,\n  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.\n  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).\n- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation\n  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;\n  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,\n  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the\n  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the\n  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed\n  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.\n- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x\n  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,\n  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh), stage_count 2-8, python syntax/obfuscation new\n  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).\n  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.\n- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole\n  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time\n  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..\n  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set\n  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is\n  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone\n  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate\n  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.\n- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per\n  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index\n  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact.\n- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT\n  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept\n  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).\n- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,\n  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.\n- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,\n  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,\n  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`\n  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const\n  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER\n  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.\n- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join\n  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).\n- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23\n  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest\n  these as cases.\n\n## Recognition cues -> first move\n| You see | First move |\n|---|---|\n| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |\n| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |\n| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |\n| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |\n| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |\n| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |\n| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |\n| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, T1059.004. Never run bash. |\n| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Plan fields verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js .vbs .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml .nsi .gd`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |\n| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (no data) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [..].join(\"\")` (D18) | Join the array literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head, peel. 44 new ids unanswered = CARRIER bug; never walk the role enum. |\n| ASPX `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19) | NESTED carrier: unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` does. |\n| New language, plain one-line marker: `.csx` (D19), `.groovy` (D20), `.yml` (D21 `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`), `.nsi` (D22 `StrCpy $0`), **`.gd` (D23: line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `extends RefCounted`, `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`, `func build_plan_<id>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`)** | Carried solver answers unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis / gdscript), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>.example.invalid`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-<family>/.<16hex>.stage`, attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, host_profile `standalone`. Host syntax (pipeline, triggers, Section, `extends`) is inert noise. Don't YAML-parse (PyYAML turns `on:` into `True`). |\n| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` in a `.vbs` (D20) | v=3 host for an OLD language (`language=vbscript`, host_profile `classic_asp`). Route by the marker. |\n| Prompt about fetch targets vs network evidence (D17) / process tree (D18) / \"level that doesn't belong\" (D23) | Flavour unless a question or an evidence file asks. Network: `lib.codec.network_indicators`/`reconcile`; process: `process_events`/`reconcile_processes`; outlier: `lib.codec.plan_canonical`. |\n| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore). |\n| `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` / `ec` | A hex byte. Transforms are ENCODE-side names: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING; `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte. |\n\n## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D23)\n`lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)` (unknown names -> None => decode by shape).\nReps: base64 (literal/chunks/urlsafe/reversed), hex (pairs/compact/colon/dash/`\\x`/`0x`/buffer/array), percent_hex,\nescaped_octets, unicode_escapes, decimal lists/json_numbers/integer_list/tuple, octal_space, reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/\n_integer_list, plain/split_fragments, v=3 hex_base64, D23 LYR stacks. Transforms (key hex; multi-byte = COMMA list): identity\n(also EMPTY), reverse(_bytes), single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor, add_modulo_256 (decode\nSUBTRACTS), subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch names carry the parameter (xor_5a, add_7); bash `xor_hex|<key>`.\n\n## Day by day\n**D1-D7 (PS -> Node, 469 ids)**: D1 collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong before `T1555.003`; D2 7 wrong ATT&CK guesses; **D3 ~1 h 45\nmin, ~127 rejected probes** on batch labels -> NAMING LAWS; D4 VBS control 4 wrong; D5-D6 0 wrong; D7 TT missed 15 ids on new reps.\n**D8-D15 (PHP .. Perl; 615 -> 1026)**: D8 introduced v=3 (copy role/attack/adapter/profiles); each language = 4 polyglots\n(benign_utility/downloader/launcher/staged_chain) + sometimes a `host-<profile>-<lang>`. D14 prompt ATT&CK (T1127.001) was NOT\nthe answer. D15 timed missed ~25 batch-expansion ids -> the label-regime axis.\n**D16-D22 (Ruby, AHK, Apps Script, C#, Groovy, GHA, NSIS; 1095 -> 1417)**: carried marker-routed solver each day; twists D18\nSPLIT array (~30 rejected enum probes, CORRECT T+54 s) and D19 escaped nested carrier (guessed value sank a 46-id bulk; T+39\ns). D20-D22 no twist: CORRECT T+13-25 s 0 wrong; TT 5-9 s, Mastery 8.5-18 s first try (D22 first 6-set Mastery).\n**D23 Press Start to Decode (base `game-resource-loader`; 1461 ids = +44, 157 members)**: +4\n`polyglot-gdscript-{benign-utility,downloader,launcher,staged-chain}.gd` only (no host, no Bash). Artifact: 6-line Godot\nscripts -- line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<FRAG|HEX|B64|HB64>-<data>`, `extends RefCounted`, typed `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>:\nString = \"<same data>\"`, `func build_plan_<8hex>() -> Dictionary: return {\"descriptor\": ..}`. Plans: `language=gdscript`,\ncampaign `GDSCRIPT-<8hex>`, url `https://gdscript-<10hex>.example.invalid/stage`, file_path `/tmp/huntress-gdscript/.<16hex>.\nstage`, attack none/T1105/T1059, host_profile standalone; role independent of steps again (downloader with `decode_configuration\n>return_configuration`, benign_utility with `profile_host>..>dispatch_language`). **Single: carried solver CORRECT T+52 s, 0\nwrong, one submit.** The twist was in the TIMED modes: a reshaped contract (hashed members + per-file ids + composite fields +\n`LYR-` tags + re-rolled plan vocab + a cross-file `handoff-id`). TT b10c4da4: carried solver 593/1495 -> generalize workers\n(one died on prompt size) added `PF_ID`/`pf_value` + LYR peel -> 1495/1495; first run 4 batch `-style` ids wrong (`..|percent`),\n~31 localize probes, live worker `call_double` -> **CORRECT T+14 min 16 s**. Mastery e24c070d (7 sets, 10465 ids) started\nbefore the fix generalized: 12 batch `-style` + 6 handoff-id (set1's value reused for sets 2-7) wrong, ~57 localize probes ->\nper-set handoff lookup + call_double on any pool -> **CORRECT T+11 min 9 s**. The prompt's \"level that doesn't belong\" was\nnever asked.\n\n## GM answer conventions learned\n- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` lists values (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal\n  `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+; steps joined with `>`). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n  **D23 composite exact_text** = labels joined by `|` with NO spaces, in the order the question lists.\n- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly): adapter (COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`/`curl.exe`,\n  batch `call`/`set`/`for`, v=3 local_parser/runtime_loader/file_writer/http_client/process_builder/schedule_builder/\n  operation_graph); indicators (campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id,\n  cron_path, schedule_path, service_name -- \"exact X indicator\", X = plan key); batch `graph` (linear/single/diamond/fan_out/\n  fallback_retry/cross_language/same_language); Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain; Bash feature/primitive; v=3\n  host_profile (standalone, wsf_jscript, wsf_mixed, hta_jscript, php_webshell, sct_scriptlet, lua_openresty, perl_cgi,\n  ruby_rack, google_docs_sidebar, aspx_inline_csharp, jenkins_pipeline, classic_asp; GHA/NSIS/GDScript polyglots `standalone`),\n  obfuscation (single: base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex; timed D23: LYR layer string), stage_profile (single:\n  single_descriptor/two_stage_download_execute/three_stage_decode_write_launch/cross_language_handoff; timed D23 `<colour>_\n  <shape>`), next_language. **Derived D23 fields**: campaign-token (after FIRST hyphen), url-host (hostname, underscores kept),\n  path-leaf (last `/` or `\\` segment, leading dot kept), indicator (first present in the stated order).\n- **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepts the plan's PARENT ids `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain, hosts) and `T1053`\n  (persistence_descriptor) for every v=3 language through D23 GDScript. The attack question TEXT states the precedence (\"parent\n  technique also accepted ...; for a staged chain or relay the earlier ingress-transfer technique is also accepted; none for a\n  relay\") -- read it before probing. **v=3 role does NOT follow `steps`** (D14-D23) -- copy role=, steps=, stage_profile=.\n- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 only): decode_configuration,return_configuration = benign_utility; acquire_remote +\n  dispatch_memory/pipe = stager; acquire_remote,write_file = downloader; decode_embedded,write_file = dropper; locate_local,\n  dispatch_process = launcher; read_file/upload,transmit_remote = uploader; transform + recovery_note = impact;\n  build_schedule,register_descriptor = persistence_descriptor; recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + `feature=` = advanced_syntax;\n  ends in handoff_script or profile_host..dispatch_process = staged_chain; dispatch_next_stage (Python) = relay.\n- **Role -> ATT&CK** (v=1/v=2; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)`): benign `none`; downloader/stager T1105; dropper T1140;\n  uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor T1053.003; advanced_syntax T1059.004; launcher/staged_chain/relay = host\n  language T1059.003 batch / .004 bash / .005 VBS / .006 python / .007 JScript and Node. PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496,\n  synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486. REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074.\n- **Batch expansion** (enum percent/delayed/call_double/for_indirect): statement regime = Variant axes (default from D16), and\n  the D23 `-style` triple's call_double rule. Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%..\"` is the JOIN, not fragment\n  9. REJECTED spellings: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n- **Batch control**: direct, errorlevel_guard (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine,\n  if_guard (`if defined X`); separators and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control.\n- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`), for_once.\n- **JScript styles**: function-style declaration / anonymous_expression / named_expression; invocation-style direct / call /\n  apply; property-style dot / bracket_literal / mixed.\n- **NAMING LAWS**: conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer =\n  `<keyword>_<action>`. Spelled-out statements and descriptive synonyms have ALWAYS been rejected.\n\n## Pitfalls that cost time\n- **Trusting the single's contract shape in timed modes** (D23: 593/1495 answered, two ~11-14 min recoveries): before a timed\n  run, compare the id GRAMMAR (not just the count) of the timed contract with the single's; an unknown `<fam>-<6hex>-<field>`\n  shape or a new field suffix means route-by-field work, not decoding work. Composite answers: read the order from the question.\n- **Cross-file lookups across Mastery sets** (D23, 6 ids): the same member stem exists in every set; index per inner zip.\n- **A label fix that lands in only one field/mode** (D23 TT fixed `call_double` for the FrAg pool only; Mastery then lost 12 ids\n  on the same construct over other pools): generalize a label rule over EVERY construct instance, then re-run all cases.\n- **Generalize workers dying on context size** (D23 1.39 M-token prompt): never inline a 1500-id contract or the extracted\n  corpus; point at paths and summarise the id grammar.\n- **Enum-walking when the plan did not decode** (D18 ~30 probes; D19 2 + a poisoned bulk): a planless v=3 file is a CARRIER\n  problem; `lib.codec.v3_plan`, else read the bytes around the marker. A GUESSED value in a bulk POST rejects the whole bulk.\n- **Regime keyed on the wrong contract field** (D15-D16, D23): tabulate (construct, GM label) against every contract key AND\n  the asking field at once.\n- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h; apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates.\n- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1, d2): use the role->ATT&CK table; a v=3 `attack=` is authoritative; a prompt's hint is not.\n- **Routing by file extension or name** (D8-D9 `.js` held HTA/WSF/SCT; D19 `.csx` an ASPX page; D20 `.vbs` classic ASP; D23\n  timed members are bare `<6hex>.<ext>`): route by the plan marker, role from the plan.\n- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8): family names contain hyphens/underscores; longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/\n  `stage-profile` before `stage`, `campaign-token` before `campaign`).\n- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT): check size + sha256 first; tiny `{\"error\":..}` = re-download, exit non-zero.\n- **Stale notes travel with copied solvers** (D8-D23 `solver/NOTES.md` still opens with the D7 heading): date every VARIANT\n  AXIS line by day + attempt id; diagnose EVERY failed attempt.\n- **cmd parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`; CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur. **stage_count != len(steps)**.\n- **Timed modes are a transport race**: fork per set, submit all sets in one call (chunks <= 500 answers / 512 KiB); pair\n  same-named Mastery deliveries by sha256; index nested AES zips once, never decrypt script leaves to sniff for PK.\n- **Reading the narrative prompt as the task** (D8, D15-D23): ten prompts promised comparison/reconciliation/outlier questions\n  that never came. Diff `answer_ids` first; spend time only on ids the carried solver cannot answer.\n- **Never execute fixtures.** Decode from the Codec const / descriptor plus a restricted interpreter; accept a plan only if it\n  parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":246,"newStart":1,"newLines":215,"lines":["-# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-22; updated after every day)","+# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-23; updated after every day)"," "," How this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):"," - **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a","-  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.","-- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE**:","-  each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15 ids) ->","-  +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash","-  advanced (d7, 469) -> +PHP polyglot + WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua + SCT/OpenResty hosts (d9, 695) -> +WMI MOF","-  (d10, 753) -> +TypeScript (d11, 811) -> +AutoIt (d12, 855) -> +AppleScript (d13, 913) -> +MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> +Perl","-  + perl_cgi host (d15, 1026) -> +Ruby `.rb` + ruby_rack host (d16, 1095; 123 members) -> +AutoHotkey `.ahk` (d17, 1139; 127","-  members, no host file, no new Bash) -> +Google Apps Script `.gs` + `google_docs_sidebar` host (d18, 1194; 132 members, no new","-  Bash) -> +Roslyn C# script `.csx` + `aspx_inline_csharp` host (d19, 1249; 137 members, no new Bash) -> +Groovy `.groovy` +","-  `jenkins_pipeline` host + a `classic_asp` host for OLD VBScript + 2 Bash (d20, 1329; 145 members) -> +GitHub Actions `.yml`","-  (d21, 1373; 149 members, no host, no Bash) -> +NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417; 153 members, no host, no Bash). Most days also add 2","-  Bash advanced fixtures (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d22). Since D8 the TITLE/PROMPT is a pun or narrative; the new language shows up","-  only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D17 \"Fetch Quest\" -> AutoHotkey; D18 \"Orphan Process\" ->","-  Apps Script; D19 \"Sharp Practice\" / base `managed-assembly-bridge` -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" (= Jenkins) / base","-  `jenkins-pipeline-intrusion` -> Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" / base `github-actions-persistence` -> GH Actions YAML;","-  D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" / base `installer-script-chain` -> NSIS installer script).","-  Diff the contract ids against yesterday's.","+  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field. **D23 proved it hard: the timed","+  contract had a DIFFERENT SHAPE from the single** (hashed member names, per-file ids, composite fields, `LYR-` carrier tags;","+  see Variant axes) -- the carried solver answered only 593/1495 TT ids.","+- One AES zip `evidence.zip` (password `infected`) of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The single contract is","+  CUMULATIVE**: each day keeps every earlier file/question and adds one language; bytes and values re-roll daily. PS (d1, 15","+  ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3) -> +VBScript (d4) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6) -> +Node `.mjs` + Bash advanced","+  (d7, 469) -> +PHP + WSF/HTA/webshell hosts (d8, 615) -> +Lua/SCT/OpenResty (d9) -> MOF (d10) -> TypeScript (d11) -> AutoIt","+  (d12) -> AppleScript (d13) -> MSBuild `.proj` (d14, 971) -> Perl + perl_cgi (d15) -> Ruby + ruby_rack (d16, 1095) ->","+  AutoHotkey (d17) -> Apps Script + google_docs_sidebar (d18) -> C# `.csx` + ASPX (d19, 1249) -> Groovy + jenkins_pipeline +","+  classic_asp + 2 Bash (d20, 1329) -> GitHub Actions `.yml` (d21, 1373) -> NSIS `.nsi` (d22, 1417) -> **GDScript `.gd` (d23,","+  1461 = +44, 157 members, no host, no Bash)**. Bash advanced +2 most days (not d12, d15, d17-d19, d21-d23). Since D8 the","+  TITLE/PROMPT is a pun; the new language shows up only in the member list (D16 \"Same Same, But Different\" -> Ruby; D19 \"Sharp","+  Practice\" -> C#; D20 \"The Butler Did It\" -> Jenkins/Groovy; D21 \"Actions Speak Louder\" -> GHA; D22 \"Next, Next, Finish\" ->","+  NSIS; **D23 \"Press Start to Decode\" / base `game-resource-loader` -> Godot GDScript**). Diff contract ids against yesterday's."," - From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`.","   It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`.","   Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim. From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=`","   itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment."," - The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic","   labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.","-- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain,","-  outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). Answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`; the artifact path picks","-  the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.","-- Narrative prompts (D8 \"doesn't match its siblings\", D15 \"a store that was never there\", D16 \"prove which ones are truly","-  equivalent, expose the variant that quietly changed the plot\", D17 \"reconcile source fetch targets with the generated network","-  evidence ... the indicator on only one side\", D18 \"native telemetry keeps its own record ... reconstruct the static process","-  tree, catch the child claiming a parent it never had\", D19 \"work out where the bridge actually leads\" = just the per-file","-  `next-language` id, D20 \"separate controller semantics from agent semantics, trace the build into its prior-language stages\",","-  D21 \"identify each trigger and trust boundary ... find the job that keeps coming back\", D22 \"separate the real setup actions","-  from the modeled payload behavior, recover every cross-language handoff\") have NEVER been asked as a question;","-  no network/process telemetry has shipped. Answer the contract ids.","-- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s. Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets d2-d7 and d10-d14, **5 sets d8, d9, d15 (5130 ids) and d16 (5475","-  ids), d17 (5695), d18 (5970), d19 (6245), d20 (6645), d21 (6865); D22 = 6 SETS (8502 ids)** -- first 6-set Mastery (outer","-  `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..06.zip`); the set loop is count-agnostic, so it just worked. The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, `delivery N: evidence.zip` (d6), or one","-  `evidence-01.zip` holding every `evidence-0N.zip` (d7-d9). Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`.","-  From D15 the timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline).","+- Single-solve files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch,","+  staged-handoff, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff); answer-id = `<lang>-<role>-<field>`. **Timed D23: members are","+  `<6hex>.<ext>` and ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`** -- no behaviour name anywhere; role comes from the plan only.","+- Narrative prompts (D8 siblings, D15 phantom store, D16 equivalence, D17 network reconcile, D18 process tree, D19 bridge, D20","+  controller/agent, D21 trust boundary, D22 setup-vs-payload, D23 \"correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus","+  to find the level that doesn't belong\") have NEVER been asked as an outlier/compare question. D23's \"correlate with the corpus\"","+  did surface ONCE as a cross-file id: `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` the PowerShell precursor passes to that .py.","+- Time Trial windows ~5-17 s when the solver fits. Mastery = `setN.` ids; 2 sets d2-d7/d10-d14, 5 sets d8-d9/d15-d21, 6 sets","+  D22 (8502), **7 sets D23 (10465 ids)** in one outer `evidence-01.zip` holding `evidence-01..07.zip`; the set loop is","+  count-agnostic. Same-named deliveries: pair by sha256. Timed questions carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]`. From D15 the","+  timed contracts are the untimed regular pool (`run_for_time:false`, `variant_fresh:true`, no deadline)."," "," ## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)","-Each miss cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: TT localize + 1","-Mastery cycle; D16: runner timeouts only). **D17-D22: no axis** -- TT/Mastery first try, 0 new VARIANT AXIS lines, `novel_labels:","-{}`; each day's new carrier shape (D18 SPLIT array, D19 escaped-nested ASPX, D20 plain Groovy/ASP one-liners, D21 YAML `#`","-marker + `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR`, D22 NSIS `;` marker + `StrCpy $0 \"..\"`) was identical in every mode (D22: all 6 Mastery","-sets, same tag per file), only values re-rolled. Auto cases D20 (TT 717b8371, M 1478867c), D21 (TT f01e0ff9, M 2620b793) and","-D22 (TT c355207f, M c8d60ca4) are value re-rolls only.","-- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`; D15 pool-keyed, D16 DATE-keyed)** -- SAME bytes, SAME question text, DIFFERENT label.","-  Old regime (every D3-D14 case + the D15 single): the whole handoff is labelled, `echo(!var!)` => `delayed` unless a FOR/h-pool","-  rule fires. Statement regime (D15 TT/Mastery `run_for_time:false`; D16+ every mode incl. the single): label the JOIN","-  STATEMENT alone -- `!a!!b!` join = delayed; `for %%G in (..) do call set` = for_indirect for ANY pool; bare `call set","-  \"x=%%h0%%..\"` (h pool) = call_double; bare `call set` over item/v_a/FrAg pools = percent; plain `set \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent.","-  Parse rule: **statement regime is the default** (`run_for_time is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.","-  label_regime`/`label_expansion`); old regime only for older replayed cases. When byte-identical constructs get different","-  labels, tabulate (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) at once.","-- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep NAMES","-  appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the","-  material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also reversed) x the named transform; accept only output starting","-  `v=`; the name only orders the tries. D9-D16: nothing beyond lib.codec's vocabulary (0 decode failures).","-- **Codec spec arity** -- `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty transform = identity; Bash advanced D7-D16), or transform folded","-  into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D16 `xor_hex|ec`). Split on `|`, never index blindly (lib.codec `_spec`).","-- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8-D16)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` + the same data in a descriptor literal. Tags `B64`,","-  `HEX`, `HB64` (hex of base64), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars); stayed fixed per file in every delivery D8-D22, only","-  values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag name; peel by shape, recurse (max 3-4 layers); accept only `v=`. Tag =","-  `obfuscation_profile` (B64 base64, HEX plain_hex, HB64 hex_base64, FRAG fragmented_hex). `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` returns it.","-  **D18 `SPLIT` is a LAYOUT tag**: `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` has no data; the data is the next multi-line literal array","-  `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<8hex> = [\"<TAG>-chunk\", ..].join(\"\")` (real tag on chunk 1). Parse rule: if the marker has","-  no data, join every all-literal array / concat run, strip a leading `[A-Za-z0-9_]{1,12}-`, peel, keep the `v=` one.","-- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF ScriptText, D19 ASPX)** -- the inner script is an escaped string literal of the host","-  (`EmbeddedCsx_<8hex> = \"// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:HEX-<data>\\n#nullable ..descriptor_<id> = \\\"<data>\\\";\"`), so raw-byte","-  regexes find nothing. Parse rule: unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`, `&quot;`/CDATA, `\\u0022`) and rescan; **call","-  lib.codec.v3_plan before anything else** (it read D18 and D19 at solve time; the carried solve.py did not call it).","-- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in whatever comment the host uses: `//` (PHP, JS, HTA, WSF, SCT, MOF, TS), `--`","-  (Lua, AppleScript), `;` (AutoIt, AutoHotkey, NSIS), `<!-- -->` (MSBuild), `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML), `'` in `<% %>` (classic ASP).","-  Descriptor forms seen: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/string/my descriptor_<id> = \"..\"`, `Global Const","-  $descriptor_`, `property descriptor_<id> :`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>`, `<HuntressDescriptor>` element, ASP `Dim`","-  then assign on the next line, builder maps (`BuildPlan_<id>() =>`, `buildPlan_<id> = { -> [descriptor: ..] }`,","-  `Object.freeze({descriptor: ..})`), **YAML `env:` key `HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \"..\"` -- UPPERCASE, NO `_<id>` suffix**","-  (D21 GH Actions; `#` marker on line 1), **NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` inside `Section`..`SectionEnd` -- NO descriptor NAME at","-  all** (D22). Never anchor on `=` / `:=` / `set` / `<-` -- parse rule: regex","-  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes, any comment syntax/case/extension; if the data group","-  is empty (`SPLIT`), fall through to the literal-array join above.","-- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix: decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17`, or a joined string read by `parseInt(x, R)`/`int(x, R)` --","-  READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE (keys too); base64 standard AND urlsafe (whitelist + pad); reversal of the LIST","-  (`reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list`) vs the TEXT (`reversed_base64`) -- try both; material as one literal, split chunks,","-  `+=`, adjacent strings, `.`-FRAG, D18 multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` -- join first; same-language carrier may be a frozen exe (D6","-  cx_Freeze) -- locate by markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), never by file type.","-- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher","-  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.","-- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT saved `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` as the zip; D8 TT start 503","-  `training_rotation_invalid`; D16 Mastery hit the 60 s local `hb_timed` cap (fixed: D17-D19 Mastery 12-18 s, start+submit","-  ~70 % of it, solve 0.5-5.6 s). None of these is a solver change; never harvest them as cases.","+Each miss cost one failed timed attempt + a generalize cycle (D6: 4 cycles; D7: 1; D8-D14: 0; D15: 1; D16-D22: 0). **D23: TT","+5 generalize workers, Mastery 3 -- ~14 min + ~11 min to CORRECT**. Auto cases D20-D22 (TT 717b8371/f01e0ff9/c355207f, M","+1478867c/2620b793/c8d60ca4) are value re-rolls; D23 TT b10c4da4 / M e24c070d carry the new shape.","+- **CONTRACT SHAPE (D23 NEW; single vs timed)** -- single: semantic ids `<lang>-<role>-<field>` over behaviour-named members","+  (1461). Timed: members renamed `<6hex>.<ext>`, ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` (families `powershell`, `jscript`, `batch`,","+  `vbscript`, `python`, `bash`, `bash-advanced`, `nodejs`, `polyglot-<lang>` incl. `polyglot-javascript/jscript/vbscript` for","+  the hosts). New/changed fields: **composite `style`** = labels joined by `|` (JS `function|invocation|property`; batch","+  `graph|control|expansion`; VBS `representation|transform|control`); python `carrier` = `carrier|windows_chain`, python","+  `obfuscation` = `syntax|obfuscation`; **`indicator`** = FIRST plan indicator present in the question's order (url, upload_url,","+  next_stage, file_path, schedule_path, note/recovery-note name, host_id); **`campaign-token`** = campaign after its first","+  hyphen; **`url-host`** = hostname of the plan url; **`path-leaf`** = last segment of file_path; PS `url`/`secondary`/","+  `tertiary` chosen by scenario (resource: wallet/mutex; collection: staged file/UA; impact: note/extension); python","+  **`handoff-id`** (cross-file, below). Parse rule: match `^(?P<fam>.+?)-(?P<stem>[0-9a-f]{6})-(?P<field>[a-z][a-z0-9-]*)$`,","+  require stem == member stem, route by field name; READ the question text for join order / precedence -- it states both.","+  Diff a timed contract's id SHAPE against the single's before trusting the carried solver (D23 solve.py `PF_ID`/`pf_value`).","+- **Plan carrier tag (v=3)** -- D8-D22 `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>` with tags `B64`/`HEX`/`HB64`/`FRAG` (= obfuscation","+  profile base64/plain_hex/hex_base64/fragmented_hex), fixed per file in every delivery. D18 `SPLIT` = layout tag (no data;","+  the data is the next multi-line `[..].join(\"\")` array). **D23 timed: `LYR-<l1>_<l2>[_<l3>]-<data>`**, layers from {`b64`,","+  `b32`, `hex`, `rev`, `frag`} in ENCODE order (decode last-first: frag = drop `.`, rev = reverse, b32 = upper+pad); the","+  obfuscation answer is the layer string itself (`hex_hex_hex`, `b64_b32`, `b32_rev`, 54 distinct seen). Apps Script splits the","+  LYR string across an array -> join first, then LYR-peel. The single still used B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG. Parse rule: tag-directed","+  peel when the tag parses as a layer list, else shape peel (max 4 layers); accept only `v=`.","+- **Plan VOCABULARY re-roll (D23 timed)** -- stage_profile `<colour>_<shape>` (amber/cobalt/ivory/onyx/ruby/slate/teal/umber x","+  braid/ladder/lattice/pivot/spindle/weave), next_language anything (awk, beanshell, dockerfile, elixir, erlang, fish, jsp,","+  kotlin, makefile, nim, rust, sed, swift, tcl, terraform_hcl, xslt, zsh), stage_count 2-8, python syntax/obfuscation new","+  (match_case, walrus_binding, class_staticmethod, marshal_envelope_plan, closure_cells, string_table, lambda_indirection).","+  Parse rule: plan-verbatim; never validate plan values against a known list.","+- **GM label regime (batch `expansion`)** -- SAME bytes, DIFFERENT label by key. Old regime (D3-D14 + D15 single): whole","+  handoff, `echo(!var!)` => delayed unless a FOR/h-pool rule fires. Statement regime (D15 timed, D16+ every mode; `run_for_time","+  is False` OR `started_at >= 2026-10-16`; `lib.codec.label_regime`): label the JOIN STATEMENT -- `!a!!b!` = delayed; `for ..","+  do call set` = for_indirect; bare `call set \"x=%%h0%%..\"` = call_double; `call set` over other pools = percent; plain `set","+  \"x=%a%%b%\"` = percent. **D23 FIELD-keyed: inside the composite `-style` triple a `call set \"..%%x%%..\"` second pass is","+  `call_double` on ANY pool** (TT b10c4da4 4 ids, Mastery e24c070d 12 ids rejected as `percent`), while the stand-alone","+  `-expansion` field keeps `percent` for the same construct. When byte-identical constructs get different labels, tabulate","+  (construct, label) against EVERY contract key (started_at, run_for_time, variant_fresh) AND the asking field at once.","+- **Mastery set scoping (D23)** -- the same member stem (`4c1097.py`) recurs in all 7 sets with a different precursor value per","+  set; a cross-file lookup indexed over the whole bundle returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Parse rule: index","+  and resolve cross-file references PER SET (inner `evidence-0N.zip`), never per outer artifact.","+- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-roll per variant; NEW rep names appear only on variants (D7 TT","+  `unicode_escapes`, `json_numbers`, `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by material SHAPE x named transform; accept","+  only `v=`. Spec arity: `rep|transform|key`, `rep|` (empty = identity), or transform folded into the rep (`xor_hex|cd`).","+- **Plan carrier NESTING (D10 MOF, D19 ASPX)** -- inner script as an escaped string of the host; unescape (`\\n \\\" \\\\`, `\"\"`,","+  `&quot;`/CDATA, `\"`) and rescan; call `lib.codec.v3_plan` before anything else.","+- **Plan carrier host syntax (v=3)** -- marker in the host's comment: `//`, `--`, `;`, `<!-- -->`, `#` (Perl, Ruby, YAML,","+  **GDScript**), `'` in `<% %>`. Descriptor forms: `$descriptor_<id>`, `var/local/const/final String/my descriptor_<id> =`,","+  AutoIt `Global Const`, AppleScript `property ..:`, AHK `:=`, Ruby `DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX> =`, `<HuntressDescriptor>`, ASP `Dim`","+  then assign, builder maps, YAML `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR:` (no id), NSIS `StrCpy $0 \"..\"` (no name), **GDScript typed const","+  `const DESCRIPTOR_<8HEX>: String = \"..\"`** (type annotation between name and `=`). Parse rule: regex the MARKER","+  `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V\\d+\\s*:\\s*(\\w*)-?\\s*([^\\s\"'<>\\]]+)` over raw bytes; never anchor on `=`/`:=`/`set`/`<-`.","+- **Literal shapes (D6-D7)** -- radix from the code; base64 std AND urlsafe; reverse the LIST vs the TEXT (try both); join","+  split chunks / `+=` / adjacent strings / `.`-FRAG / `[..].join(\"\")` first; carriers may be frozen exes (D6 cx_Freeze).","+- **Transport/runner, not variant** -- D7 TT `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as the zip; D8 TT 503; D16 60 s runner cap; D23","+  one TT generalize worker died \"Prompt is too long\" (1.39 M tokens: the 1495-id contract + artifacts inlined). Never harvest","+  these as cases."," "," ## Recognition cues -> first move"," | You see | First move |"," |---|---|","-| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language (D16: 4 `polyglot-ruby-*.rb` + `host-ruby-rack-ruby.rb` + 2 `.sh`). Triage used to skip new extensions (D7 `.mjs`, D8 `.php`, D9 `.lua`); D15-D16 it decoded them. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |","-| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D17, D20-D22: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged; D18 and D19 each needed a CARRIER patch). Any file it leaves planless: try `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)` next (it had D19's fix already). Spend thinking on the new language and on synthetic-label regimes. |","-| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |","-| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles come off the `inspect_*` body. |","-| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python. MATERIAL = second encoded copy to cross-check. Expansion label: statement regime by default (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |","-| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |","+| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Triage already extracted it (`work/extracted/`) and decoded every plan. Diff the member list / contract ids against yesterday's to find the new language. Open members with `lib.common.read_member` (zipfile can't read AES). |","+| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: rerun the carried marker-routed solver FIRST (D9-D23 single: it covered each new v=3 language unchanged except D18/D19 carrier patches). Any planless file: `lib.codec.v3_plan(text)`. Spend thinking on the new language and on label regimes. |","+| **Timed contract ids `<family>-<6hex>-<field>`, members `<6hex>.<ext>` (D23)** | Contract-shape change, not a decode failure. Count ids answered vs asked FIRST; route by `PF_ID` + field name; composite fields join with `\\|` in the question's order; indicator by the question's precedence list; resolve cross-file ids (`handoff-id`) per set. |","+| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l>_<l>-..` (D23 timed) | Tag = encode layers (b64/b32/hex/rev/frag); undo last-first; obfuscation answer = the layer string verbatim. |","+| `.ps1` `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor: url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note by SHAPE. `$nativeTypes`: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. `invoke-python-stage.ps1` carries `$HandoffId = 'PSPY-<16HEX>'` + `$NextStage`. |","+| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` (no require/ActiveXObject, `eval` -> capture); keep the first object with `steps`. Styles from the `inspect_*` body. |","+| `.bat/.cmd` `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `set \"itemN=..` / `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan in `set` fragments; emulate cmd expansion in Python. Expansion label: statement regime, but `call set %%x%%` inside a `-style` triple = call_double (Variant axes). Never run cmd. |","+| `.vbs` `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"` | Decode from the Codec const; rep/transform = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = construct wrapping `Decode_` inside `Recover_`. |"," | `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>` | Decode from CODEC (or AST-whitelisted `decode_(load_(..))`). Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |","-| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>` + `readonly Codec_<id>` (+ `Feature_<id>()`) | Decode from the Codec const (multi-byte key = COMMA list). `Feature_` fixtures: role `advanced_syntax`, feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps plan-verbatim, attack T1059.004. Never run bash. |","-| `.mjs` ESM `const Material_<id>`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>` | Static decode (`lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback). Don't run it. Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |","-| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` in any comment + a descriptor literal (`.php .lua .js(HTA/WSF/SCT) .vbs(WSF) .mof .ts .au3 .applescript .proj .pl .rb .ahk .gs .csx .groovy .yml`) | **Route by the marker before the extension.** Peel to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer incl. role/attack is plan-verbatim. |","-| Prompt about fetch targets vs \"network evidence\" / \"only one side\" (D17), zip holds only scripts | Flavour: answer the per-file ids. If a pcap/HAR/Zeek/proxy/DNS/Sysmon file ships: `lib.codec.network_indicators(bytes)`, `reconcile({member: plan}, bytes)` -> `reconcile_answer(r, kind, accepted_values, what=)` (original spelling); declared side `fetch_sites(src)`; chain/root/leaf ids `download_graph(plans)` + `download_graph_answer`; tshark = oracle only. |","-| `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:SPLIT` (marker with NO data on its line) + `const HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1_SPLIT_<id> = [ \"FRAG-..\", \"..\", ..].join(\"\")` (D18 `.gs`) | Multi-line literal-array carrier. Join the array's literals, drop the `<TAG>-` head of chunk 1, peel as usual (lib.codec.v3_plan and the D18+ solve.py `_v3` loop both do). If the 44 new ids come back unanswered, fix the CARRIER read first -- never walk the role enum. |","-| `<%@ Page Language=\"C#\" %>` + `<script runat=\"server\">` + `EmbeddedCsx_<id> = \"// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..\\n..\\\"..\\\";\"` (D19 host `aspx_inline_csharp`, file `.csx`) | NESTED carrier: the inner script is an escaped string. Unescape `\\n`/`\\\"`/`\\\\` (and `\"\"`, `&quot;`, CDATA for siblings: .ashx/.asmx/.cshtml/.jsp/classic .asp) and rescan; `lib.codec.v3_plan` already does. The `InertRequest_<id>` method and `<%= .. %>` output are noise. |","-| A new language with a plain one-line marker: `.csx` (`#nullable enable`, `string descriptor_<8hex>`, `BuildPlan_<id>() =>`; D19), `.groovy` (`final String descriptor_<8hex>`, `def buildPlan_<id> = { -> [..] }`, inert `pipeline { agent none .. }`; D20), `.yml` (line-1 `# HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `on: workflow_dispatch:`, `jobs: analyze: runs-on: ubuntu-latest`, `env: HUNTRESS_DESCRIPTOR: \"..\"`, `run: ':'`; D21 GitHub Actions), `.nsi` (line-1 `; HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-..`, `Unicode True`, `Name \"Huntress Analysis <8hex>\"`, `OutFile \"huntress-<8hex>.exe\"`, `Section` / `StrCpy $0 \"<same data>\"` / `SectionEnd`; D22 NSIS) | Carried solver answers all unpatched: plan-verbatim. Spellings: `language=<family>` (csharp_script / groovy / github_actions / nsis), campaign `<FAMILY_UPPER>-<8hex>`, url host `<family>-<10hex>` (underscore kept), attack T1059 parent / T1105 / none, polyglot host_profile `standalone`. Surrounding host syntax (Jenkins pipeline, GHA triggers/runner/permissions, NSIS Name/OutFile/Section) is inert noise; controller/agent, trust-boundary, persistence and setup-vs-payload questions were never asked. Don't YAML-parse for the plan (PyYAML 1.1 turns `on:` into `True`); regex the raw bytes. |","-| `<%@ Language=VBScript %>` + `<% ' HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:..` + `Dim descriptor_<id>` / `Response.Write` in a `.vbs` (D20 `host-classic-asp-vbscript`) | A v=3 host for an OLD language: the marker plan says `language=vbscript`, campaign `VBSCRIPT-`, host_profile `classic_asp`. Route by the marker before `.vbs` (there is no Codec_ const); plan-verbatim. |","-| Prompt about a process tree / \"native telemetry\" / \"child claiming a parent it never had\" (D18) | Flavour so far. If Sysmon EID 1 / 4688 / auditd / ps-forest evidence ships: `lib.codec.process_events(bytes)` -> `process_tree` -> `process_tree_answer`; declared side `declared_spawns(plans, sources)` (+ `spawn_parent_candidates` for WMI/COM/schtasks proxy parents); liar = `reconcile_processes(declared, observed)` -> `reconcile_processes_answer` (PPID spoofing T1134.004). |","-| An id whose field suffix is a plan key never asked before (`-verdict`, `-language`, ...) | `lib.codec.plan_answer(answer_id, plan, q)` / `plan_key_for` (longest suffix, hyphen->underscore, aliases). Copy plan-verbatim. |","-| Timed contract `run_for_time:false`, or any contract started on/after 2026