dnfile; no csv/ast/shlex/marshal). Priority-1 order for D24:\nwhat actually cost D23 (timed per-file contract grammar in lib, tag-directed LYR peel with wider layer names, corpus\ncross-file / stage-chain correlation incl. the never-asked \"level that doesn't belong\", field-keyed composite labels), then the\ntitle thread (game-engine script languages, Godot resources/packs, game archives), then the installer leftovers.\n\n'''\nP=lambda **k:k\nnew=[\n P(id=\"per-file-hashed-contract\", concept=\"timed per-file contract grammar: `<family>-<6hex>-<field>` ids over `<6hex>.<ext>` members with composite / derived fields\", priority=1, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"D23 TT/Mastery reshaped the contract (single kept semantic ids); the carried solver answered 593/1495. Move D23 solve.py PF_ID/pf_value into lib: lib.codec.pf_route(answer_id, question, members)->(family, member, field); pf_answer(field, plan, question, kind)-> value for composite style (JS function|invocation|property, batch graph|control|expansion, VBS representation|transform|control), python carrier (carrier|windows_chain) and obfuscation (syntax|obfuscation), indicator by the precedence list PARSED FROM THE QUESTION TEXT (not hard-coded), campaign-token (after first hyphen), url-host, path-leaf, PS secondary/tertiary keyed by scenario. Also accept unknown 4-8 hex stems and future fields via plan_answer. Test on challenges/day23/scripting-press-start-to-decode/solver/cases/variant-time_trial-b10c4da4 and variant-mastery-e24c070d (GM-verified).\"),\n P(id=\"lyr-tag-layer-peel\", concept=\"tag-directed layered carrier peel: `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:LYR-<l1>_<l2>_..-<data>` with today's and likely next layer names\", priority=1, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"D23 timed tags listed ENCODE layers from {b64,b32,hex,rev,frag} (1-3 deep, 54 combos); obfuscation answer = the layer string. Put lib.codec.lyr_peel(tag, data) in lib with tolerant names for the next 'power-up': b64u/urlsafe, b32hex, b58, b85/a85/z85, gz/gzip, zlib/deflate, bz2, xz/lzma, rot13/rotN, xor<hex>, url/pct, uu, qp, utf16, rev, frag; up to 6 layers; a tag mismatch falls back to shape peel; accept only v=. Wire into v3_plan so SPLIT arrays carrying a LYR head (D23 Apps Script) also peel.\"),\n P(id=\"corpus-stage-correlation\", concept=\"corpus cross-file correlation: precursor->next-stage links, handoff ids, stage chains, and the odd member out\", priority=1, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"D23 asked `python-<6hex>-handoff-id` = the `$HandoffId` that invoke-python-stage.ps1 passes to that .py (`$NextStage`, `--handoff-id` ArgumentVector); Mastery lost 6 ids by resolving it across sets. Prompt: 'correlate its stage relationships with the rest of the corpus to find the level that doesn't belong'. Build lib.codec.corpus_links(members:{name: text}, plans) -> edges (src, dst, via: next_stage|file_path|handoff_id|next_language|url) scoped to ONE set, link_value(dst, key) for 'what does X pass to Y' questions, and stage_outlier(plans, edges) -> member whose declared next_language/stage_count/stage_profile/steps disagree with its siblings or whose link target is missing; answers in original spelling.\"),\n P(id=\"game-script-language-route\", concept=\"game-engine / modding script languages as the next v=3 polyglot (Luau, Ren'Py, GML, Squirrel, AngelScript, Pawn, mcfunction, UnrealScript, Unity C#, LÖVE Lua)\", priority=1, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"D23 'Press Start to Decode' / base game-resource-loader = GDScript; the lane adds one sibling per thread (AutoIt->AHK, Jenkins->GHA). Fixture battery per language with the D8 4-file polyglot shape, verify lib.codec.v3_plan reads each comment/descriptor form: Luau `-- ` + `local DESCRIPTOR_X: string = \\\"..\\\"`; Ren'Py `# ` + `define descriptor_x = \\\"..\\\"` / `$ x = ..` in `init python:`; GML `// ` + `#macro DESCRIPTOR_X \\\"..\\\"` / `global.x = ..`; Squirrel `// ` + `local x = @\\\"..\\\"` (verbatim, `\\\"\\\"` escape); AngelScript `const string x = ..`; Pawn `new const x[] = \\\"..\\\"` + `\\\\` escapes; mcfunction `# ` + `data modify storage huntress:x set value \\\"..\\\"`; UnrealScript `var string x; defaultproperties { x=\\\"..\\\" }`; Unity C# `[SerializeField] string x = ..`.\"),\n P(id=\"godot-resource-pck-carrier\", concept=\"Godot resource containers: `.tscn`/`.tres` embedded GDScript (`script/source = \\\"..\\\"`), `.pck` packs, `.gdc` tokenized scripts\", priority=2, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"A 'resource loader' twist would move the D23 .gd into a Godot resource: `[sub_resource type=\\\"GDScript\\\" id=..]` with `script/source = \\\"<escaped source>\\\"` (escapes \\\\n \\\\t \\\\\\\" ) -> nested-carrier unescape then V3_MARK. `.pck`: magic GDPC, u32 pack ver, engine ver, reserved, file count, entries (path len+path, offset u64, size u64, md5) -> extract text members (.gd/.tscn/.tres/.cfg/.json) without running anything; `.gdc` (Godot 3 tokenized) -> string-table extract. lib.codec.godot_members(data)->[(path, bytes)].\"),\n P(id=\"game-archive-carriers\", concept=\"other game archives as script carriers: Ren'Py `.rpa`/`.rpyc`, LÖVE `.love`, Unity TextAsset bundles, RPG Maker `plugins.js`\", priority=2, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"`.rpa` RPA-3.0 header `RPA-3.0 <hexoffset> <hexkey>` -> zlib-compressed pickle index (offset/len XOR key) -- parse with a RESTRICTED pickle reader that allows only dict/list/tuple/str/bytes/int (no find_class); `.rpyc` `RENPY RPC2` slot table -> zlib chunk -> string literals only (no unpickle of AST classes). `.love` = zip of .lua; Unity `UnityFS` bundle -> LZ4 blocks -> TextAsset strings (scan for HUNTRESS markers); RPG Maker `js/plugins.js` `$plugins = [..]`. Output: [(path, text)] for the marker scan.\"),\n P(id=\"composite-label-field-regime\", concept=\"synthetic labels keyed by the asking FIELD (composite `-style` triple vs stand-alone field)\", priority=2, action=\"prebuild\",\n   detail=\"D23: batch `call set \\\"..%%x%%..\\\"` = call_double inside `graph|control|expansion` (TT 4 + Mastery 12 ids rejected as percent) but percent in the stand-alone `-expansion` field. Extend lib.codec.label_expansion(construct, regime, field=) with a field axis and a tabulator: label_table(cases_dir) -> {(construct, field, regime): {label: n}} from expected.json + gm_feedback.json, flagging any construct whose label differs by field; same treatment for JS styles and VBS control inside composites.\"),\n]\ngaps=new+[keep[i] for i in (\"linux-package-maintainer-scripts\",\"macos-pkg-installer-scripts\")]\ngaps.append(P(id=\"mastery-set-scope\", concept=\"resolve every cross-file reference inside its own Mastery set\", priority=1, action=\"note\",\n   detail=\"D23 Mastery e24c070d: `4c1097.py` existed in all 7 sets; a bundle-wide index returned set1's handoff id for sets 2-7 (6 rejected). Index per inner evidence-0N.zip; cases must keep set-distinct values.\"))\ngaps.append(P(id=\"timed-contract-shape-diff\", concept=\"diff the timed contract's id grammar against the single's before trusting the carried solver\", priority=1, action=\"note\",\n   detail=\"D23: single = semantic ids, timed = per-file hashed ids + composite fields; answered/asked dropped to 593/1495 and cost ~25 min across TT+Mastery. A pre-run check (answered ratio < 0.98 on a fresh contract => generalize offline before submitting) would have caught it; workers must not inline the 1500-id contract (one generalize worker died at 1.39 M tokens).\"))\nfor i in (\"solver-lib-v3-fallback\",\"php-cli\",\"lua-unluac\",\"xsltproc-cabextract-yq\",\"leaf-ext-list\",\"new-synthetic-label-family\",\"family-name-underscore\"):\n    g=keep[i]\n    if i==\"leaf-ext-list\": g=dict(g); g[\"detail\"]=g[\"detail\"].replace(\".yml .nsi\", \".yml .nsi .gd\") if \".gd\" not in g[\"detail\"] else g[\"detail\"]\n    gaps.append(g)\ngaps.append(P(id=\"godot-re-tools\", concept=\"Godot pack/bytecode extractor\", priority=2, action=\"tool\",\n   detail=\"gdsdecomp (GDRE Tools) release binary into tools/gdre (headless: `gdre_tools --headless --recover=x.pck --output-dir=out`); only for .pck/.gdc/.exe Godot exports; never run the game. Static lib reader (godot-resource-pck-carrier) covers plain packs.\"))\ngaps.append(P(id=\"unrpyc\", concept=\"Ren'Py .rpyc decompiler\", priority=3, action=\"tool\",\n   detail=\"git clone https://github.com/CensoredUsername/unrpyc into tools/unrpyc; it unpickles (code execution risk) -- run only under python3 -I in the sandbox on copies, prefer the restricted lib reader.\"))\nfor i in (\"tcl-r-interpreters\",\"applescript-scpt\",\"js-deob-extras\",\"ps-deob-modules\",\"xlm-standalone\",\"dotnet-script\"):\n    gaps.append(keep[i])\nfor g in gaps: assert set(g)=={\"id\",\"concept\",\"priority\",\"action\",\"detail\"}, g[\"id\"]\nassert len({g['id'] for g in gaps})==len(gaps)\njs=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g, ensure_ascii=False) for g in gaps)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(js)\nt=t[:a]+prose+\"```json\\n\"+js+t[e:]\nopen(p,'w').write(t)\nprint(len(gaps), sum(1 for g in gaps if g['action']=='prebuild'))\nPYEOF\ntail -c 300 reference/coverage/script-analysis.md; wc -l reference/coverage/script-analysis.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":559,"cache_read_input_tokens":178236,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":559},"output_tokens":58,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2434f37c-0f23-47a1-8221-7c3852d69d0d","uuid":"061acb1f-8a3b-45e6-8481-27093b18d7bf","timestamp":"2026-10-23T13:36:55.881Z","request_id":"req_011CgKFv9p6jBSDWuZRwnfwL","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B1nwdsUxeA8z74CqgDdELK":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; python3 - <<'PYEOF'\nimport json\np='reference/coverage/script-analysis.md'\nt=ope